{"beat_id":"HUNT_04_CROWN_PROTOTYPE_B016","speaker_id":"","text":"","left":{},"right":{},"active_side":"none","advance_mode":"manual","cues":{"implementation_flags":["SOURCE_STAGING"],"source_section":"6. ARENA ENTRY","staging":"Player gets a final preparation prompt before entering. - formation; - equipment; - items; - save/recovery available outside; - **no mandatory Vaelira battle slot**; - any legal four-character formation must be viable. The arena gate closes behind the party using a simple prepared door-state swap. The Crown Prototype activates. No long cinematic. No speech. No transformation sequence. **HUNT — CROWN PROTOTYPE**"}},
{"beat_id":"HUNT_04_CROWN_PROTOTYPE_B017","speaker_id":"","text":"","left":{},"right":{},"active_side":"none","advance_mode":"manual","cues":{"implementation_flags":["SOURCE_STAGING"],"source_section":"Core concept","staging":"A **single-target combat prototype built around repeated attack correction**. It is not an elemental mini-Crucible. It does not repeat S024's six-element gimmick. Its gameplay identity is: **miss → adjust → reacquire → strike repeatedly** This naturally supports the Relentless Flurry reward without claiming the defeated enemy somehow creates the Card."}},
{"beat_id":"HUNT_04_CROWN_PROTOTYPE_B018","speaker_id":"","text":"","left":{},"right":{},"active_side":"none","advance_mode":"manual","cues":{"implementation_flags":["SOURCE_STAGING"],"source_section":"Structure","staging":"- **One enemy** - **One HP bar** - **No transformation** - **No summoned support units** - **No mandatory character** - **No Prime requirement** - **No scripted round gimmick** - **No immunity puzzle** - Stronger than surrounding Chapter 4 enemies but clearly below a Major Hunt."}},
{"beat_id":"HUNT_04_CROWN_PROTOTYPE_B019","speaker_id":"","text":"","left":{},"right":{},"active_side":"none","advance_mode":"manual","cues":{"implementation_flags":["SOURCE_STAGING"],"source_section":"Retained technical baseline","staging":"- Lv. 11 - HP: 1,505 - EXP: 280 - CEXP: 50 - Auren: 120 - Historical tuning reference: approximately 4–7 rounds depending on build/party Those numbers remain balance targets rather than narrative scripting."}},
{"beat_id":"HUNT_04_CROWN_PROTOTYPE_B020","speaker_id":"","text":"","left":{},"right":{},"active_side":"none","advance_mode":"manual","cues":{"implementation_flags":["SOURCE_STAGING"],"source_section":"CALIBRATION STRIKE","staging":"Single-target physical attack. Basic pressure move. Clean readable animation using the Prototype's normal attack rig."}},
{"beat_id":"HUNT_04_CROWN_PROTOTYPE_B021","speaker_id":"","text":"","left":{},"right":{},"active_side":"none","advance_mode":"manual","cues":{"implementation_flags":["SOURCE_STAGING"],"source_section":"TARGET ACQUISITION","staging":"The Crown Prototype marks one party member. Until its next major sequence: - increased Accuracy against that target; - target is visibly identified through an inexpensive reticle/status icon. No unavoidable damage. Player can defend, protect, heal, debuff, or simply race it."}},
{"beat_id":"HUNT_04_CROWN_PROTOTYPE_B022","speaker_id":"","text":"","left":{},"right":{},"active_side":"none","advance_mode":"manual","cues":{"implementation_flags":["SOURCE_STAGING"],"source_section":"RELENTLESS SEQUENCE","staging":"Three or four physical hits. Normally prioritizes the acquired target, but later hits may redirect if that target is incapacitated. This is the boss's signature attack pattern. It **does not award or activate Relentless Flurry during battle**. The similarity is thematic only."}},
{"beat_id":"HUNT_04_CROWN_PROTOTYPE_B023","speaker_id":"","text":"","left":{},"right":{},"active_side":"none","advance_mode":"manual","cues":{"implementation_flags":["SOURCE_STAGING"],"source_section":"CORRECTIVE STEP","staging":"If one of the Prototype's attacks misses or is evaded, it gains a temporary Accuracy increase. The machine is visibly correcting for failure. This keeps high-evasion parties useful without allowing permanent trivialization. The correction expires normally."}},
{"beat_id":"HUNT_04_CROWN_PROTOTYPE_B024","speaker_id":"","text":"","left":{},"right":{},"active_side":"none","advance_mode":"manual","cues":{"implementation_flags":["SOURCE_STAGING"],"source_section":"BREAKLINE","staging":"Heavy single-target physical blow. Moderate chance to lower Defense for a short duration. Used less frequently than its multi-hit sequence. Provides a reason to respond rather than simply heal through repeated small hits."}},
{"beat_id":"HUNT_04_CROWN_PROTOTYPE_B025","speaker_id":"","text":"","left":{},"right":{},"active_side":"none","advance_mode":"manual","cues":{"implementation_flags":["SOURCE_STAGING"],"source_section":"9. SAME-BAR ESCALATION","staging":"At lower HP, the Prototype does **not transform**. Its existing lights brighten. Movement cadence increases. Cheap battle-state change only. It gains: **ACCELERATED TEST CYCLE** - slightly higher Speed; - more frequent Target Acquisition → Relentless Sequence combinations; - no HP refill; - no free threshold attack; - no new body/model; - no Prime refresh. The player remains in the same battle continuously."}},
